    "created_at": "2015-10-08T19:03:02Z",
    "updated_at": "2015-10-08T19:03:02Z",
    "body": "Given that `type`, `bubbles` and `cancelable` already have to be mutable for all events, is there any additional harm in having the remaining members of `MessageEvent` be mutable?\n\nPerhaps this would be clearer with an example of a patch adding or removing an `init*Event()` method to Servo.\n\nI also take it this isn't an issue with Gecko.\n",
    "author_association": "MEMBER",
